  </ActionButton>
 
   <IntakeGate ready="!@interdisciplinary_1_completion_page.value">
   <Markdown> </Markdown>
   <Vertical>   
  <!-- ORIENTATION -->
    <SplitPanel id="interdisciplinary_orientation" title="Introduction" sizes="65,35">
      <LeftPane>
          <Markdown id="interdisciplinary_orientation_md">
**Introduction**

Imagine that as part of your degree requirements, you are completing an internship at a local
nonprofit called **Community 360**, or **Comm360** for short.

The mission of Comm360 is to address community-based needs and issues through responsive
programming in multiple areas such as:
 - Education and Training
 - Health and Welfare
 - Family and Youth Services
 - Community Building and Advocacy

A community needs survey conducted by Comm360 identified the high rate of students dropping out
of high school in the area as a serious issue. You have been asked to work with other interns
to investigate the causes of high school dropout to better understand the problem so that
Comm360's services can be developed to address the problem.
          </Markdown>
      </LeftPane>
      <RightPane>
          <Image id="interdisciplinary_image" src="/sba/interdisciplinary/images/nonprofit.png" alt="Nonprofit" />
          <Image id="interdisciplinary_image2" src="/sba/interdisciplinary/images/wordcloud.png" alt="Helping, volunteer, community, donations ..." />
      </RightPane>
    </SplitPanel>

    <Image id="interdisciplinary_gsu_plaza_image" 
         src="/sba/interdisciplinary/images/GSU_Library_Plaza.jpg" 
         alt="GSU Library Plaza. Photograph by Hwi Padam, CC by SA 4.0" 
         height="400px"
    />

    <Markdown id="interdisciplinary_task_list">
## Task Outline

In the next 45-60 minutes you will work with your teammates to complete the following tasks:
 1. _Brainstorm causes for high school dropout._
 2. _Review community focus group data._
 3. _Select Focus Areas._
 4. _Reflect: Is this an interdisciplinary problem?_
 5. _Review the literature._

This is Part One. In Parts Two and Three you will complete the rest of the interdisciplinary
research process.
    </Markdown>

    <Image id="cause_brainstorming" 
         src="/sba/interdisciplinary/images/team_workshop.jpg"
         height="400px"
         alt="Talking about processes at a team brainstorming session. Source: UCT MOOC, CC by SA 4.0 International License" />

    <Markdown id="internal_and_structural_causes">
## Internal and Structural Causes

 - **Internal Causes** arise from **inside** the student;
     for instance, they may get sick and be unable to keep up with the work.
 - **Structural Causes** arise from **outside the student**, from the way
     their family, community and school are structured and organized;
     for instance, the school may not provide any support for sick
     students that would enable them to continue their classes by
     independent study.
    </Markdown>

